Title: Night Delivery
Credit: Written by
Author: Sample Writer
Draft date: 2026-09-01

INT. WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

A single work lamp swings over stacked crates. FAISAL crouches behind a pallet, breathing hard. Torchlight sweeps the far wall.

FAISAL
(whispering)
Two minutes. Then we move.

EXT. WAREHOUSE LOADING BAY - NIGHT

Rain hammers the concrete. A van idles, headlights cutting through the downpour. The camera tracks with FAISAL as he sprints the length of the bay and slides under the shutter.

INT. VAN - MOVING - NIGHT

Handheld, tight. NOURA drives one-handed, watching the mirrors. Dashboard light paints half her face green.

NOURA
You said two minutes.

EXT. DESERT HIGHWAY - DAWN

Wide. The van is a speck on a ribbon of asphalt, the sun breaking over the escarpment. A drone shot pulls up and back until the vehicle disappears into the landscape.

INT. ROADSIDE CAFE - DAY

Fluorescent tubes, tiled walls, hard flat light. FAISAL counts notes under the table while NOURA watches the door.

FAISAL
It's short.

NOURA
It's what he gave me.

EXT. ESCARPMENT RIDGE - DUSK

Golden hour. A long crane move rises off the two figures standing at the edge, revealing the valley behind them.
